cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below, and also cite the original NASA sources listed in docs/sources.md."
title: "Before the First Fire on the Moon: evidence on how spacecraft materials burn in partial gravity"
abstract: >-
  A decision-support tool and curated evidence set built for the NASA Space Apps
  Challenge 2026 (Flame in Freefall). It compiles NASA flammability tests in
  microgravity, partial gravity and Earth gravity, with every value traced to its
  source document and page, to show which materials may behave differently on the
  Moon ahead of NASA's FM2 (Flammability of Materials on the Moon) experiment.
type: software
